<title>UK: SBC sets call, put warrants on 13 U.S stocks.</title>
<headline>SBC sets call, put warrants on 13 U.S stocks.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss Bank Corp has issued call and put warrants of five million per series on 13 U.S. stocks, lead manager SBC Warburg said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>There are two tranches of call and one tranche of put warrants on each of Barrick Gold Corp, Amgen Inc, Boeing Company, Cisco Systems Inc, The Walt Disney Company, General Electric Company, Hewlett-Packard Company, International Business Machines Corp, McDonald's Corp, Philip Morris Cos Inc, Motorola Inc, Merck &amp; Co Inc and Texaco Inc.</p>
<p>Maturity date for all the warrants is October 7, 1998 and payment date is July 22, 1997. They are listed on the Luxembourg stock exchange and are available in minimum exercise lots of 1,000.</p>
<p>--London newsroom,  +44 171 542 7658</p>
